## page_crud Tool - Page Management with Puck Visual Builder

The `page_crud` tool manages pages within Puck apps.

### Methods
| Method | Description | Required Params |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| list | List pages in app | app_id |
| read | Get page by ID | page_id |
| create | Create page | app_id, data.name |
| update | Update page metadata | page_id, data |
| update_content | Update Puck content | page_id, data.templateData |
| publish | Make page public | page_id |
| unpublish | Make page private | page_id |
| delete | Delete page | page_id |

### Page Fields
- `id`: Unique page identifier
- `appId`: Parent app ID
- `name`: Display name
- `slug`: URL-friendly identifier
- `description`: What the page shows
- `order`: Position in navigation (number)
- `templateData`: **Puck visual content (JSON)** - see structure below
- `isPublic`: Whether page is published
- `requiresAuth`: Whether login is required
- `allowedRoles`: Array of role names for access control

### Puck templateData Structure

The `templateData` field contains the visual page content in Puck format:

```json
{
  "root": {
    "props": { "title": "Page Title" }
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "Hero",
      "props": {
        "title": "Welcome",
        "description": "Your hero section text",
        "buttons": [{"text": "Get Started", "href": "/start"}]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Cards",
      "props": {
        "items": [
          {"title": "Feature 1", "description": "..."},
          {"title": "Feature 2", "description": "..."}
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "zones": {}
}
```

### Available Puck Blocks

| Block | Purpose | Key Props |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| Hero | Header section with title and CTA | title, description, buttons, backgroundImage |
| Cards | Grid of feature cards | items[], columns |
| Text | Rich text content | text, align |
| Heading | Section heading | text, level (h1-h6) |
| Image | Image with caption | src, alt, caption |
| Button | CTA button | text, href, variant |
| Columns | Multi-column layout | columns[] |
| VerticalSpace | Spacing element | size |
| Flex | Flexible container | direction, gap, items[] |
| Stats | Statistics display | items[] with value, label |
| Logos | Logo grid | logos[] with src, alt |

### Example: Creating a Landing Page

```python
# Create page with Puck content
page_crud(
    method="create",
    app_id=1,
    data={
        "name": "Home",
        "slug": "home",
        "templateData": {
            "root": {"props": {"title": "Home"}},
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "Hero",
                    "props": {
                        "title": "Welcome to Our Product",
                        "description": "The best solution for your needs",
                        "buttons": [{"text": "Get Started", "href": "/signup"}]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "Cards",
                    "props": {
                        "items": [
                            {"title": "Feature 1", "description": "Description of feature 1"},
                            {"title": "Feature 2", "description": "Description of feature 2"},
                            {"title": "Feature 3", "description": "Description of feature 3"}
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ],
            "zones": {}
        }
    }
)
```

### Example: Update Existing Page Content

```python
# Update existing page content
page_crud(
    method="update_content",
    page_id=5,
    data={
        "templateData": {
            "root": {"props": {"title": "Updated Page"}},
            "content": [...],  # New Puck content
            "zones": {}
        }
    }
)
```

### Response Format (TOON)
- Success: `page:created,5,Home,home` or `pages|3]{id,name,slug,isPublic}:...`
- Failure: `FAILED: error message`
